Group 3 -  Diagnostic Evidence Team (DET)
 Member 1 (Pediatric Pathologist (Lead)): Reviews and interprets the blood smear and any additional tissue analyses necessary to assess for any hematological abnormalities and provide a definitive diagnosis.
 Member 2 (Geneticist): Evaluates the potential for inherited bleeding disorders by reviewing family history, testing for genetic markers associated with conditions like Glanzmann’s thrombasthenia or Bernard
 Member 3 (Pediatric Infectious Disease Specialist): Assesses any infectious etiologies that may contribute to the bleeding or bruising and advises on necessary additional laboratory tests to rule out conditions like thrombocytopenic conditions secondary to infections.

Group 4 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Pediatric Hematologist (Lead)): Provides expert guidance in the interpretation of test results and collaborates with the MDT to formulate a diagnosis and treatment pathway, considering all findings.
 Member 2 (Clinical Pediatric Pharmacist): Reviews treatment options and medication management involved in the care of the diagnosed condition (e.g., potential treatments for bleeding disorders) and ensures appropriate dosing and monitoring.
 Member 3 (Pediatric Social Worker): Supports the family in navigating the healthcare system, addressing psychosocial aspects resulting from the child's condition, and coordinating care resources for ongoing management and education.


